<h1>Big Tech &amp; Startups</h1>
<h3>OpenAI launches cheaper reasoning model (4 minute read)</h3>
<p>OpenAI on Tuesday launched a reasoning model that costs $2 per million input tokens, about 60% less than the model it replaces. It is live in the API today and comes to ChatGPT next week, according to the company.</p>
<h3>Rust in the Linux kernel passes a milestone (6 minute read)</h3>
<p>The Linux kernel now ships more than 100 Rust drivers. Maintainers say memory-safety bugs in those drivers have dropped sharply, and two major distributions will enable the Rust toolchain by default next year.</p>
